# Runtime Skills

Runtime Skills execute concrete tasks.

A runtime skill may contain:

- when to use;
- procedure;
- tool and connector requirements;
- scripts and templates;
- validation gates;
- pitfalls and recovery steps.

A runtime skill must not embed:

- private user facts;
- long-term preferences;
- raw evidence;
- project memory that belongs in `identity/memories/`.

This LifeOS does not use `identity/wenxin/skill-recommendations.yml` as a real Skill directory. Candidate Skills first enter `identity/wenxin/skill-recommendations.yml`; they enter `capabilities/<skill-id>/` only after a real `SKILL.md` exists.

Put fact dependencies in `identity/cognition/skill-bindings/data-sources.yml`.
